4. APPROACH A: THE LIMITER W135 SELECTED WITH A REPLACEMENT REGULATOR FOUND ON PRINTED FIGURES
   the limiter: TI TPS2553-1 (DBV), RILIM 49.9 kOhm 1 %: IOS 0.4702 to 0.5878 A (MODEL: the PRINTED row 0.475 to 0.565 A, the resistor's 1 % through
     the equations' exponents, W135's band); latch-off after 5 to 10 ms (PRINTED); response 2 us TYPICAL only (never used as a limit)
   the regulator's requirements at the 14.0k corner (W135's method on W159's envelope): junction-to-ambient at most 95.7 C/W; output and current limit
     at least 0.5878 A; input to at least 4.1174 V; dropout at 0.5878 A that keeps T10-A3 with its own output band (below)
   the regulators read, each at the limiter's maximum 0.5878 A from the corner (MODEL on the PRINTED rows; the dropout INFERRED linear from 1 A):
     part                                           C/W    TJ (C)   VDO (V)    A3 need  A3 margin  verdict
