     (the supply at the LDO's input at 0.5878 A on all three: 3.6036 V, record l9t5's path with the limiter's 0.135 ohm PRINTED; the adjustable parts carry
     a 0.1 % divider's 0.2 % beside the maker's band, an ASSUMPTION: their sheets exclude the resistors; TLV757P's band is printed at 1 mA only)
   SELECTED within A: TPS73733DCQRM3. Its junction at the limiter's maximum 115.0 C (10.0 K under 125 C; it holds to 95.7 C/W, 26 % over the
     printed 76.0 C/W); the M3 order code fixes the new silicon, whose dropout and band qualify where the legacy silicon's do not
     the alternate within A: TPS73701DRBRM3 (VSON-8 3 x 3 mm, 49.4 C/W) with a 0.1 % divider, if board B's pocket refuses the SOT-223
   A, row by row (the selected pair; MODEL on PRINTED unless labelled):
   (1) THE WINDOW: IOSmin 0.4702 A over every served state (largest S3' 0.4240 A: +0.0462 A; (f1) 0.3726 A: +0.0976 A; S2 0.2839 A; S1 0.1855 A): no served
       state is limited, so no bridging capacitance and no timer restart is relied on; the TCAN334's 180 mA row is inside (f1). Row 8's
       (f2) 0.5491 A and rev V's held 0.5639 A lie inside the band (0.4702 to 0.5878 A): a supervisor there MAY be limited and latched off after
       5 to 10 ms, before FW-B21's 100 ms response; row 8's accepted outcome ('nothing moves', the voters at the home assignment) is
       the same with it, and the supervisor returns only when EN or power is cycled (a new failure mode, (7))
   (2) THE REGULATOR'S JUNCTION at 76.25 C air on its PRINTED 76.0 C/W: at the limiter's maximum 0.5878 A, 115.0 C (holds 125 C for every waveform
       under the limit: a constant-power bound, the cx46 countermodel's periodic peaks included); at S1 0.1855 A, 88.5 C; the realisation of the
       printed figure on board B's copper is a Layer 10 means (JEDEC 2s2p, 3×2 vias under the tab): read at E-17's coupon, never assumed
       its ground current (880 uA TYPICAL at 1 A, no maximum printed) is outside the bound: 3.6 mW at the top input, 0.28 K on the printed
       theta (MODEL on a TYPICAL), against the 10.0 K margin
       the limiter's own junction in service at 0.5878 A: 84.8 C (0.135 ohm, 182.6 C/W, PRINTED); its continuous rating 1.2 A to 125 C TJ PRINTED
   (3) THE OUTPUT SHORT: (i) a short above the regulator's foldback draws the limit and latches within 10 ms (PRINTED): at most 24.2 mJ (MODEL);
       (ii) a hard short folds the TPS737 back to its own short-circuit current, 0.510 A TYPICAL only, which may sit under IOSmin: the limiter
       may not act; W135-2's exclusion carried (SESSION W138-3): the supervisor on a shorted rail is lost (IOHA row 3), the other two keep
       their supply (each branch at most IOSmax), and the regulator's survival rests on its PRINTED 'Output short-circuit duration: Indefinite'
       (SBVS067W 5.1), not on a typical shutdown; its junction during (i) is not computed (no transient thermal impedance printed)
       the same exclusion covers a partial short on the supervisor's own 3.3 V that pulls its output out of regulation while drawing under
       IOSmin (the drop then exceeds the corner's): (2)'s bound is stated for the output in regulation, every served state's case
   (4) T10-A3 with the limiter's 0.135 ohm and the TPS737's PRINTED band (+1.5 %) and dropout (0.250 V at 1 A, INFERRED linear):
       (a) at T10's point 0.2452 A on all three               3.6936 V against 3.4108 V: +0.2828 V, holds
       (b) at the limiter's maximum 0.5878 A on all three     3.6036 V against 3.4965 V: +0.1072 V, holds
       (c) S1 0.1855 A at the other two, one at the limiter's maximum 3.6921 V against 3.3959 V: +0.2963 V, holds
       (e) S3' 0.4240 A on all three in one bit               3.6466 V against 3.4555 V: +0.1911 V, holds
       (f) with round 6's 0.3 ohm sense (+1 %) kept in series, at the limiter's maximum: 3.4255 V against 3.4965 V: -0.0710 V, FAILS (SESSION W138-2)
       (d) U601 and the lead's pin 1 at three maxima: 1.7634 A against 3 A and 10 A (PRINTED, T10 line 272): holds
       the band's own condition: the TPS737's +-1.5 % is PRINTED for VIN >= VOUT + 0.5 V (5.6); the input here is 3.6466 to 3.7579 V at the served
       currents, under 3.8495 V: the band between VOUT + VDO and VOUT + 0.5 V is INFERRED (the AP2112's was tested at 4.3 V, T10's same gap):
       V-T10-DROP extended (finding L4REG-F2)
   (5) PARTS AND AREA (MODEL on the makers' package outlines; board B's floor plan gen_pcb_b3.py):
       per supervisor, A against the tree: the LDO's land 8.1 to 45.9 mm2 and one SOT-23-6 with two 0603 resistors and one 0603 capacitor:
       +49.7 mm2; against round 6's drafted state (the rail trip's eight parts, 25.1 mm2, removed): +24.6 mm2. Pocket IOCB/IOCC 1624 mm2 (gen_pcb_b3.py
       line 218), IOHA's estimate about 650 mm2 a controller (line 224): 3.1 % of the pocket, 7.7 % of the estimate; placement is Layer 10's
       (the region lists carry no part of any P0 draft yet, round 6's included: finding L4REG-F6). Parts: two ICs and three passives a
       supervisor in place of round 6's two ICs and six passives; order codes owed (finding L4REG-F4)
   (6) HO-E: unchanged by A. The H743's VOS0 105 C current 0.1936 A and its 125 C current 0.328 A depend on its own 45 C/W and the air, not
       on the regulator; IOSmin 0.4702 A sits over both, so no current limit of this stage holds the controller (W127 finding 2, L4A-59):
       the largest served S1 0.1855 A against VOS0's 0.1936 A is a 4.4 % band no limiter's printed tolerance reaches; A neither narrows nor widens it
   (7) NEW FAILURE MODES: a latched limiter (row 8, or any overload over IOSmin for 5 ms) leaves its supervisor dark until EN or power is
       cycled (nothing in this draft drives EN: the peers' restart is L4A-54's or L4A-58's, finding L4REG-F3); the limiter's latent loss of
       its limit (HO-D, L4A-58: FAULT asserts only while limiting); the legacy silicon fitted under a code without M3 (T10-A3 then fails at
       the limiter's maximum: Layer 6 and Layer 12 identity rows, finding L4REG-F4); the TPS737's start-up into foldback and its overshoot
       note (DESCRIBED; INFERRED not triggered: the limiter's output rises within 1.5 ms PRINTED at its test load, the start-up load is the
       controller in reset; first-article items, finding L4REG-F2); and the given-up average bound of round 6's rail trip on the controller's
       own current (0.2183 to 0.2452 A, PROVISIONAL, its response withdrawn): a firmware outside FW-B20 is bounded by no hardware (finding L4REG-F7)
   A's verdict on its rows: HOLDS (the judge of section 8)

5. APPROACH B: K1, A BUCK PER SUPERVISOR (board B's AP63203WU-7, as U25; record l9t5 T10 section 8)
   (1) THE INPUT: the AP63203's recommended input starts at 3.8 V (PRINTED), UVLO rising 3.30 to 3.70 V; at the 14.0k set point its input
       is at most 3.7579 V even with no current (the pre-regulator's least 3.9063 V, the rail's budget and the return's shift): UNDER the
       recommended range. K1 needs R602 back to 10.7 k (I-03's 4.87 to 5.13 V band): board A's iocpre and iocset withdrawn, Slot A's
       L9T5-D9 reversed, a cross-board change
   (2) THE THERMAL: the AP63203 prints 89 C/W (PRINTED) but no maximum on-resistance (125 and 68 mOhm TYPICAL, Note 8) and no guaranteed
       efficiency (curves only): its loss has no printed bound. On the DECLARED 0.88 at S3' 0.4240 A: 0.191 W lost, junction 93.2 C (MODEL on a
       TYPICAL: NOT a bound). K1 holds no served state limited (no limit under 2.5 A, PRINTED peak minimum), so the window is every row
   (3) THE OUTPUT SHORT: hiccup, 2 ms at the peak limit then 16 ms off (DESCRIBED, no limits), 2.5 to 3.1 A peak (PRINTED): a periodic
       waveform of up to 3.1 A at the switch drawn from +5V_IOC, shared with the other two: no printed containment per branch without a
       limiter ahead of it (A's limiter added to K1: the buck's input transients against a latch-off limit, not computed)
   (4) T10-A3: replaced by the buck's own input range ((1)): FAILS at 14.0k, holds at 10.7 k
   (5) AREA: +23.5 mm2 a supervisor against the tree (MODEL: XAL4020 inductor, bootstrap, input and two output capacitors; 1.4 % of the
       pocket), +35.5 mm2 with A's limiter for containment; switching ripple on each controller's VDD and VDDA, not computed
   (6) HO-E: unchanged (no current limit at the controller's currents)
   (7) NEW FAILURE MODES: the hiccup's periodic waveform; the switch node beside the CAN transceivers and the crystal; board A's set point
       reversed; the controller's 125 C current 0.328 A covered by nothing, as in A
   B's verdict: NOT SUPPORTED ON PRINTED FIGURES (its thermal rests on a TYPICAL efficiency; its input is under the recommended range at the
     drafted set point; no printed per-branch containment); kept as the fallback W135 named

6. APPROACH C: THE REGULATOR'S OWN PRINTED CURRENT LIMIT AS THE CONTAINMENT (no separate limiter; one part, no latch)
   the best thermal path read, the TPS737 (76.0 C/W DCQ, 49.4 C/W DRB, PRINTED), prints its limit 1.05 to 2.20 A (5.6): at the limit's maximum
   the junction reads 221.2 C (DCQ) and 170.5 C (DRB) from the corner's drop alone (the limit is printed at VOUT 90 % of nominal, a larger drop):
   OVER 150 C. A part would need a printed maximum under 1.138 A (DRB) with a minimum over S3' 0.4240 A, a 45.7 % band; and its output short
   rests on a foldback printed TYPICAL only (0.510 A), with no printed timer: unbounded. TLV757P likewise (1.20 to 1.78 A, its best 92.5 C/W)
   C's verdict: FAILS (2) and (3) on printed figures; not taken

7. THE COMPARISON AND THE SELECTION
   row                       A (TPS2553-1 + TPS73733DCQRM3)         B (K1, AP63203 per supervisor)        C (the LDO's own limit)
   window, served rows       none limited (IOSmin +0.0462 A)          none limited                          none limited
